{
  "_": [
    "One rule, stated in two languages, pinned to one table.",
    "",
    "`keel/libs/check_evidence.py` decides what a CI reports; ",
    "`keel/dashboard/modules/evidence.js` decides what the Evidence page shows. ",
    "Two implementations of one rule drift, and the way they drift is silent: ",
    "the page says an artefact is good while the check says it expired. ",
    "Both suites read this file and assert their own side of it, so a ",
    "divergence fails a test instead of reaching a user.",
    "",
    "The vocabulary is deliberately the smaller one. The dashboard also ",
    "distinguishes `due soon`, which is a warning a page can afford and a ",
    "command cannot; it collapses to `current` here.",
    "",
    "Generated once from the Python implementation and checked against the ",
    "JavaScript one; edit by hand, as a specification, not by regenerating."
  ],
